// Case keys: one line per case, in the harness's own case order (the index
// idtc_case_N and IDTC_N use), ahead of the harness C:
//
//   // idtc key N KEY [f]
//
// KEY is a decimal hash of everything the case's result can depend on in
// the source -- its own tokens, and the hashes of the components of its
// function and of every function its tokens name (a `given` setup, a `then`
// check, a `calls` target, a function passed as a value) -- or one of two
// words: `std`, a case of the standard library, which the harness never runs
// here (bin/idc's library pre-check does); or `-`, a case that must run on
// every build, because it carries a scaling claim (judged against the other
// cases carrying it), or reaches a volatile native or builtin (the clock, the
// environment, a process, a window, a write: what no hash here can see). A KEY
// followed by ` f` is a case whose only natives are file-pure
// (compiler/parse/conf.id cache_file_natives): it is keyed, and bin/idc also
// records the files it read and reruns it when one of them changes. bin/idc
// keeps a case's pass under its KEY and adds what the hashes here cannot know:
// the compiler, cc and the
// host. The conf.id constants a case reads are in the hashes here (graph/build/
// consts/).
//
// The lines are C comments, so the harness compiles as it did.

dg_emit_keys() {
  dg_build();
  int dgc = 0;
  while(dgc < len((import casefn))) {
    dg_emit_key(dgc);
    dgc = dgc + 1;
  }
} return void;
given dg_t_parsed ():() then calls dg_emit_key:[4]
given env_init ():() then calls dg_emit_key:[0]

dg_emit_key(int dgc) {
  string dgkey = dg_case_key(dgc);
  print("// idtc key " + dgc + " " + dgkey);
} return void;
given dg_t_built (0):() then prints:("// idtc key 0 -5465788173469261037\n")
given dg_t_built (3):() then prints:("// idtc key 3 -26172764691117968\n")

dg_case_key(int dgc) {
  string dgkey = "std";
  if(case_is_std(dgc) == 0) {
    dgkey = dg_case_word(dgc);
  }
} return string dgkey;
given dg_t_built (1):("1931614673935473091")
given dg_t_std (1):("std")
